1
00:00:39,550 --> 00:00:41,823
Between 2017 and 2023,

2
00:00:41,873 --> 00:00:46,237
Manchester City didn't just
win English football.

3
00:00:46,287 --> 00:00:47,940
They owned it.

4
00:00:48,255 --> 00:00:51,100
Five Premier League titles in six seasons.

5
00:00:51,389 --> 00:00:53,540
A hundred points in a single campaign.

6
00:00:53,859 --> 00:00:59,740
More than a billion euros spent
building Pep Guardiola's dream squad.

7
00:01:00,023 --> 00:01:04,413
While the traditional giants were cutting
costs and struggling in the transfer

8
00:01:04,463 --> 00:01:05,187
market,

9
00:01:05,237 --> 00:01:07,820
City seemed to live in a
different reality.

10
00:01:08,105 --> 00:01:09,809
They won everything,

11
00:01:09,859 --> 00:01:11,501
and on top of that,

12
00:01:11,551 --> 00:01:15,009
they kept announcing record
commercial revenues,

13
00:01:15,059 --> 00:01:18,580
outearning clubs with far
bigger global fanbases.

14
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:22,380
It looked too good to be true.

15
00:01:22,687 --> 00:01:24,380
It was.

16
00:01:24,694 --> 00:01:26,895
After years of investigation,

17
00:01:26,945 --> 00:01:30,971
Manchester City was found guilty
of 114 financial breaches:

18
00:01:31,021 --> 00:01:32,553
inflated accounts,

19
00:01:32,603 --> 00:01:36,082
sponsorships that weren't what
they claimed to be,

20
00:01:36,132 --> 00:01:38,820
and documents hidden from regulators.

21
00:01:39,119 --> 00:01:43,685
And none of it would have come out
if it weren't for one man,

22
00:01:43,735 --> 00:01:47,431
sitting thousands of
kilometers from Manchester,

23
00:01:47,481 --> 00:01:52,180
with a computer and 3.4 terabytes of
leaked confidential files.

24
00:01:56,246 --> 00:01:58,077
November 2015.

25
00:01:58,127 --> 00:02:03,380
The phone of FC Twente's
president won't stop ringing.

26
00:02:03,674 --> 00:02:09,089
Journalists want answers about confidential
documents that have just appeared on a

27
00:02:09,139 --> 00:02:11,700
website hosted on a Russian server.

28
00:02:11,984 --> 00:02:16,260
They're Twente's secret contracts with an
investment fund called Doyen Sports.

29
00:02:16,541 --> 00:02:21,511
In exchange for five million euros
to rescue its finances,

30
00:02:21,561 --> 00:02:27,900
the club had sold percentages of seven
players' economic rights to the fund.

31
00:02:28,209 --> 00:02:33,700
It's called third-party ownership,
T.P.O., and it's banned.

32
00:02:34,014 --> 00:02:37,211
But the worst part was a single clause.

33
00:02:37,261 --> 00:02:42,394
If Twente turned down a transfer offer
that Doyen wanted to accept,

34
00:02:42,444 --> 00:02:44,950
the club owed a massive fine.

35
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,820
In practice, Doyen was the
one running the club.

36
00:02:49,125 --> 00:02:54,546
The Dutch federation banned Twente from
European competition for three years,

37
00:02:54,596 --> 00:02:57,700
with penalties that nearly bankrupted it.

38
00:02:58,001 --> 00:03:00,380
In the months that followed,

39
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:06,520
the same source leaked tax-avoidance schemes
involving stars like Cristiano Ronaldo

40
00:03:06,570 --> 00:03:08,274
and José Mourinho,

41
00:03:08,324 --> 00:03:12,660
plus the files that would later
bring down City's empire.

42
00:03:16,703 --> 00:03:18,936
Behind that mountain of data,

43
00:03:18,986 --> 00:03:24,180
and the panic spreading through Europe's
boardrooms, there was just one name.

44
00:03:24,472 --> 00:03:27,180
Rui Pedro Gonçalves Pinto.

45
00:03:27,481 --> 00:03:29,118
Born in Portugal.

46
00:03:29,168 --> 00:03:31,076
A young FC Porto fan.

47
00:03:31,126 --> 00:03:34,990
A history student with no
formal training in tech.

48
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:37,420
He taught himself computing.

49
00:03:37,724 --> 00:03:38,911
In 2015,

50
00:03:38,961 --> 00:03:44,940
living in Budapest under the alias
"John", he launched Football Leaks.

51
00:03:45,227 --> 00:03:46,171
His goal:

52
00:03:46,221 --> 00:03:50,614
expose how football had been taken over
by shadowy investment funds,

53
00:03:50,664 --> 00:03:52,660
tax evasion and corruption.

54
00:03:52,976 --> 00:03:57,444
By breaking into servers and
running phishing attacks,

55
00:03:57,494 --> 00:04:02,180
Rui gathered more than 70 million
confidential documents.

56
00:04:02,494 --> 00:04:05,305
Too much for one person to read.

57
00:04:05,355 --> 00:04:10,097
So he partnered with European
Investigative Collaborations,

58
00:04:10,147 --> 00:04:11,457
the E.I.C.,

59
00:04:11,507 --> 00:04:15,820
a journalism consortium led by
Germany's Der Spiegel.

60
00:04:16,132 --> 00:04:18,402
As the stories exploded,

61
00:04:18,452 --> 00:04:20,431
Rui became a target,

62
00:04:20,481 --> 00:04:27,100
hunted by billion-dollar funds and threatened
by the power networks inside football.

63
00:04:31,152 --> 00:04:34,940
At home in Portugal, the leaks
hit like an earthquake.

64
00:04:35,254 --> 00:04:41,353
They exposed internal Benfica emails pointing
to alleged influence over refereeing,

65
00:04:41,403 --> 00:04:44,123
favoritism inside the federation,

66
00:04:44,173 --> 00:04:48,380
and privileged access to
confidential judicial reports.

67
00:04:48,690 --> 00:04:53,980
The scandal triggered corruption
investigations into club officials.

68
00:04:54,298 --> 00:04:58,740
But the line between activism
and crime got crossed.

69
00:04:59,039 --> 00:05:04,480
Rui tried to get one million euros from Doyen
in exchange for not publishing the

70
00:05:04,530 --> 00:05:05,353
files,

71
00:05:05,403 --> 00:05:08,660
something he'd later call a
childish mistake.

72
00:05:08,947 --> 00:05:10,148
In January 2019,

73
00:05:10,198 --> 00:05:12,025
he was arrested in Budapest,

74
00:05:12,075 --> 00:05:15,100
extradited to Portugal and
charged with 147 crimes.

75
00:05:15,417 --> 00:05:16,820
In court,

76
00:05:16,870 --> 00:05:20,409
he called himself a whistleblower,

77
00:05:20,459 --> 00:05:24,340
someone acting in the public interest.

78
00:05:24,641 --> 00:05:26,895
And to reduce his sentence,

79
00:05:26,945 --> 00:05:32,820
he handed his encrypted hard drives to
authorities in France, Belgium and Germany.

80
00:05:33,135 --> 00:05:36,900
What was on them was a lot more
than harmless chatter.

81
00:05:40,952 --> 00:05:47,580
The files showed Europe's biggest clubs
operating in a world with no rules.

82
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:49,018
In 2018,

83
00:05:49,068 --> 00:05:55,503
Football Leaks published the emails that
revealed the plans for a European Super

84
00:05:55,553 --> 00:05:56,609
League,

85
00:05:56,659 --> 00:06:03,020
a closed tournament designed by the
continent's richest clubs to make billions.

86
00:06:03,315 --> 00:06:05,651
At Paris Saint-Germain,

87
00:06:05,701 --> 00:06:10,807
after spending over 400 million
euros on Neymar and Mbappé,

88
00:06:10,857 --> 00:06:17,580
the documents exposed crude accounting tricks
to get around Financial Fair Play.

89
00:06:17,879 --> 00:06:22,835
PSG signed an inflated deal with
the Qatar Tourism Authority:

90
00:06:22,885 --> 00:06:26,462
officially worth 200 million euros a year.

91
00:06:26,512 --> 00:06:30,380
UEFA's auditors valued it at
around 3 million.

92
00:06:30,665 --> 00:06:32,025
In other words,

93
00:06:32,075 --> 00:06:37,420
state money was being pumped into the club
and dressed up as commercial revenue.

94
00:06:37,709 --> 00:06:44,165
Other files revealed a network of offshore
companies used by Cristiano Ronaldo to

95
00:06:44,215 --> 00:06:48,478
shield more than 150 million
euros in image rights,

96
00:06:48,528 --> 00:06:52,060
which led to his tax conviction in Spain.

97
00:06:52,368 --> 00:06:59,708
Der Spiegel also published documents on the
rape allegation made by Kathryn Mayorga

98
00:06:59,758 --> 00:07:03,362
against Ronaldo in Las Vegas in 2009,

99
00:07:03,412 --> 00:07:08,397
including a 375,000 dollar
confidentiality settlement.

100
00:07:08,447 --> 00:07:15,300
Ronaldo has always denied the allegation,
and no criminal charges were filed.

101
00:07:15,610 --> 00:07:18,236
But among all those scandals,

102
00:07:18,286 --> 00:07:21,780
one club kept showing up again and again.

103
00:07:22,082 --> 00:07:24,780
Manchester City.

104
00:07:28,838 --> 00:07:33,727
The man behind City's 2008
takeover is Sheikh Mansour,

105
00:07:33,777 --> 00:07:37,312
a member of Abu Dhabi's royal family,

106
00:07:37,362 --> 00:07:40,817
Deputy Prime Minister of the U.A.E.,

107
00:07:40,867 --> 00:07:42,808
and head of ADUG,

108
00:07:42,858 --> 00:07:49,500
a state-linked investment vehicle backed by
hundreds of billions of dollars.

109
00:07:49,804 --> 00:07:54,700
He also owns City Football Group, today
chaired by Khaldoon Al Mubarak.

110
00:07:55,008 --> 00:07:55,981
In 2011,

111
00:07:56,031 --> 00:07:58,797
UEFA introduced Financial Fair Play:

112
00:07:58,847 --> 00:08:02,060
clubs couldn't spend more
than they earned.

113
00:08:02,351 --> 00:08:06,740
The Football Leaks emails showed
that City's main sponsor,

114
00:08:06,790 --> 00:08:08,288
Etihad Airways,

115
00:08:08,338 --> 00:08:11,786
a company owned by the Abu
Dhabi government,

116
00:08:11,836 --> 00:08:15,620
was officially paying 67.5
million pounds a year.

117
00:08:15,928 --> 00:08:21,889
But emails from City's own finance director
admitted Etihad was only paying 8

118
00:08:21,939 --> 00:08:23,020
million.

119
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:25,803
The other 59.5 million?

120
00:08:25,853 --> 00:08:30,580
It came straight from ADUG,
the Sheikh's own fund.

121
00:08:30,873 --> 00:08:32,807
In the Guardiola era,

122
00:08:32,857 --> 00:08:35,681
the scheme got more sophisticated.

123
00:08:35,731 --> 00:08:39,171
City Football Group bought
Girona in Spain,

124
00:08:39,221 --> 00:08:43,140
in partnership with Pere
Guardiola, Pep's brother.

125
00:08:43,447 --> 00:08:49,840
Then the hunt for artificial revenue reached a
whole new level with the Wega case.

126
00:08:49,890 --> 00:08:50,985
In 2015,

127
00:08:51,035 --> 00:08:56,784
City announced a 40 million pound
sponsorship with this supposed tech and

128
00:08:56,834 --> 00:08:58,860
payment-card company.

129
00:08:59,170 --> 00:09:03,099
When journalists checked
the company records,

130
00:09:03,149 --> 00:09:05,051
they found a sham.

131
00:09:05,101 --> 00:09:06,553
No products.

132
00:09:06,603 --> 00:09:08,955
No registered employees.

133
00:09:09,005 --> 00:09:10,307
No assets.

134
00:09:10,357 --> 00:09:11,883
Total equity:

135
00:09:11,933 --> 00:09:13,460
1,200 pounds.

136
00:09:13,767 --> 00:09:15,575
At the height of it,

137
00:09:15,625 --> 00:09:20,684
City sold its players' image rights to
a third-party finance company,

138
00:09:20,734 --> 00:09:21,746
Fordham.

139
00:09:21,796 --> 00:09:23,139
From then on,

140
00:09:23,189 --> 00:09:26,523
Fordham paid those
millions to the players,

141
00:09:26,573 --> 00:09:31,500
and the cost magically vanished from
the reports City sent to UEFA.

142
00:09:31,787 --> 00:09:33,314
February 2020:

143
00:09:33,364 --> 00:09:37,975
UEFA banned City from European
competition for two years.

144
00:09:38,025 --> 00:09:39,481
Months later,

145
00:09:39,531 --> 00:09:42,421
the ban was overturned on appeal,

146
00:09:42,471 --> 00:09:46,580
and the club got away with a
10 million euro fine.

147
00:09:46,872 --> 00:09:47,841
Then,

148
00:09:47,891 --> 00:09:49,095
in 2026,

149
00:09:49,145 --> 00:09:50,819
a new verdict,

150
00:09:50,869 --> 00:09:54,111
this time from the Premier League.

151
00:09:54,161 --> 00:09:59,990
City was found guilty of 114 of the
115 charges brought against it.

152
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:06,260
The club denied every accusation and
continues to insist it is innocent.

153
00:10:10,327 --> 00:10:14,046
The 115 charges show something bigger:

154
00:10:14,096 --> 00:10:19,700
football has become hostage to
diplomacy and state interests.

155
00:10:20,008 --> 00:10:25,310
British government documents showed that the
embassy in Abu Dhabi and the Foreign

156
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:29,340
Office in London were following
the City case step by step.

157
00:10:29,653 --> 00:10:30,926
The U.A.E.

158
00:10:30,976 --> 00:10:33,719
is a giant investor in the UK,

159
00:10:33,769 --> 00:10:39,820
with more than 10 billion pounds in
energy, real estate and infrastructure.

160
00:10:40,103 --> 00:10:47,900
Truly punishing City could mean risking a
diplomatic crisis, and that money.

161
00:10:51,966 --> 00:10:56,642
One more powerful figure played a
central role behind the scenes:

162
00:10:56,692 --> 00:10:58,260
Gianni Infantino.

163
00:10:58,543 --> 00:11:00,686
According to Rui Pinto,

164
00:11:00,736 --> 00:11:06,839
the FIFA president knew about these backroom
manipulations and even held secret

165
00:11:06,889 --> 00:11:10,588
meetings to soften the
punishments for clubs.

166
00:11:10,638 --> 00:11:13,700
Infantino has denied any wrongdoing.

167
00:11:14,012 --> 00:11:17,720
Poking that hornet's nest came
at a very high price.

168
00:11:17,770 --> 00:11:22,166
Rui Pinto spent years in Portugal's
witness protection program,

169
00:11:22,216 --> 00:11:27,740
but lost that status in October of this year,
leaving him exposed to real danger.

170
00:11:28,034 --> 00:11:33,993
What actually decides the leagues and titles
that generate billions of euros are

171
00:11:34,043 --> 00:11:37,202
deals far more political than sporting.

172
00:11:37,252 --> 00:11:39,387
Deals that feel distant,

173
00:11:39,437 --> 00:11:42,186
or even like conspiracy theories,

174
00:11:42,236 --> 00:11:47,580
made by powerful people who put
themselves above the rules and the law.

175
00:11:47,895 --> 00:11:49,421
But in the end,

176
00:11:49,471 --> 00:11:53,533
all it took was one guy with an
internet connection,

177
00:11:53,583 --> 00:11:56,685
and journalists free to do their jobs,

178
00:11:56,735 --> 00:12:01,140
to prove that when a project
looks too good to be true...

179
00:12:01,455 --> 00:12:03,500
maybe it really is.
